shape theory.prior-reference : theory.continuity, theory.structure, theory.character {
  type: theorem
  layer: 0
  """
// Theorem 3.7 (Mandatory Prior-State Reference).
// The transformation producing M' must be determined in part by
// the prior moment's character.
//
// Continuity requires that M' relate to M as "the same thing in a
// new state." Structure S is shared by all moments of the same shape
// (it is constant). Therefore S alone cannot specify which prior
// moment M' continues from. The specific state is the character C.
// Without dependence on prior character, M' would be determined by
// S alone, making it the same regardless of which prior state obtained.
//
// Derives from: theory.continuity (requires connection to specific M),
//               theory.structure (S alone is insufficient),
//               theory.character (C distinguishes specific states)
  """
}
